From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WorkBuddy diagnostics
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:17:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: subsystem_restart: skip coupled restart for esoc0

enuma (SM8250 + external SDX55M) running the elish (WiFi-only) ROM has no
matching modem EFS / calibration data.  The external modem errfatals with

    ssr:MP:critical_protect.c:1721:CRITICAL_DATA_CHECK_FAILED

every ~12.9 seconds.  Each errfatal calls subsystem_restart_dev() with
restart_level = RESET_SUBSYS_COUPLED ("RELATED"), which shuts down / powers
up esoc0 and the coupled wlan subsystem, drops the cnss IMS/COEX QMI
services, and restarts com.android.phone / TelephonyNetworkProvider.

When EasyTether (communication sharing) is active the wlan is in STA + P2P
concurrency (virp2p).  The next SSR cycle tears down the STA:

    [1404.645386] ext-mdm soc:qcom,mdm0: mdm_errfatal: mdm sent errfatal interrupt
    [1404.726895] wlan: wlan0(vdevid-0): Received Disconnect reason:3
                        WLAN_REASON_DEAUTH_LEAVING
    [1404.762863] wlan: Disconnect reason: 3 ... LG: 1

i.e. the tablet's own WiFi is dropped the moment communication sharing is
connected.  Pure stock (SDX55M=OFFLINE) has no such loop, so WiFi and
sharing coexist there.

Keep esoc0 out of the coupled restart path.  The modem stays powered and its
QMI_LOC channel stays available for GNSS (the reason the GPS fix powers the
X55 up in the first place); only the endless shutdown/powerup loop that
resets wlan / cnss / telephony is suppressed.

Runtime alternatives were verified NOT to work on this kernel:
  * /sys/module/subsystem_restart/parameters/disable_restart_work = 1 or 2
    -> still "Restart sequence requested for esoc0, restart_level = RELATED."
  * /sys/bus/msm_subsys/devices/subsys10/restart_level = "disabled"
    -> read-only, reads back RELATED.
Hence a build-time change is required.

NOTE FOR APPLYING: hunk line numbers vary between 4.19 msm branches.  If
`git apply` rejects the hunk, locate the anchor manually with

    grep -n "restart_level = %s" drivers/soc/qcom/subsystem_restart.c

and insert the three-line block immediately after that pr_info() and before
the `if (disable_restart_work == DISABLE_SSR)` check.  See README.md.

---
 drivers/soc/qcom/subsystem_restart.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/subsystem_restart.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/subsystem_restart.c
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/subsystem_restart.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/subsystem_restart.c
@@ -1900,6 +1900,18 @@ int subsystem_restart_dev(struct subsys_device *dev)
 
 	pr_info("Restart sequence requested for %s, restart_level = %s.\n",
 		name, restart_levels[dev->restart_level]);
+
+	/*
+	 * enuma + elish-ROM quirk: the external SDX55M has no matching EFS /
+	 * calibration and errfatals every ~13 s.  A coupled ("RELATED")
+	 * restart here resets the wlan subsystem and the cnss IMS/COEX QMI
+	 * services, which locally deauthenticates the WiFi STA whenever
+	 * EasyTether (virp2p + STA/P2P concurrency) is active.  Keep the
+	 * modem up for GNSS/QMI_LOC, but do not run the coupled restart.
+	 */
+	if (!strcmp(name, "esoc0")) {
+		pr_warn("subsys-restart: skipping coupled restart for %s\n", name);
+		return 0;
+	}
 
 	if (disable_restart_work == DISABLE_SSR) {
 		pr_warn("subsys-restart: Ignoring restart request for %s\n", name);
-- 
2.39.0
